--prefix
fl-Oz
--name
fl-engine-Oz
--description
lifted FL Studio engine (decision 0129 final configuration; variant Oz; one configuration (decision 0243); prune-list=prune-SM.tsv; hybrid=U)
--host-files
emscripten-6.0.12
--brotli-quality
11
--bucket
fl-web-assets
--args
/data/FLEngine_x64.dll /data/dsp_ippv2_x64.2000000.dll:/data/Blend2D.4700000.dll:/data/quickfontcache_x64.1d00000.dll:/data/freetype_x64.4b00000.dll:/data/ILTools_x64.6000000.dll:/data/oggio_x64.c000000.dll:/data/elastique_x64.b000000.dll:/data/fruity_filter_x64.7000000.dll:/data/fruity_delay2_x64.7800000.dll
--env
FLE_VFS_SEED=/data/seed/vfs-seed-idle1.tsv
--env
FLE_VFS_SEED_ROOT=/data/seed
--env
FLE_REG_SEED=/data/seed/reg-seed-nsis.tsv:/data/seed/reg-seed-app.tsv
--env
FLE_AUTH_CLAIMS=/data/seed/authenticode-claims.tsv
--env
FLE_FRUITY_MAX_CALLS=4000000000
--env
FLE_FRUITY_SECONDS=36000
--fruity-hints
first=53,stop=59,variant=Oz
--stop-note
indirect call to 0=>The engine called address 0: a function it asked GetProcAddress for came back 0. Decision 0136 section 7 read this wall (after the welcome wizard is closed) as user32!UpdateLayeredWindow of the layered window TLightweightLayeredControl. Decision 0140 gave the engine a model of it, so a bundle built from a tree with that decision does not stop here. It stopped by design; the desktop shows the last picture of each window.
--stop-note
pruned function=>This build leaves out the IPP CPU variants that the fixed CPUID answer should never reach (prune list prune-SM.tsv). The engine reached one of them, so that leave-out is wrong for this run.
--out
lift/out-app/bundle
--engine-wasm
lift/out-app/web/engine.wasm
--glue
lift/out-app/web/engine-glue.js
--seed-pack
lift/out-app/seed/seed.bin
--dll-dir
lift/out-app/dll
